## 1. RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation)

### Mục tiêu

Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) là một pattern kết hợp retrieval systems với LLMs để generate responses dựa trên retrieved information. RAG giúp LLMs access current information, reduce hallucinations, và provide cited answers.

### Nguyên tắc

**1. Document Processing Pipeline**

Clean and normalize documents. Split into appropriate chunks. Preserve metadata. Handle various formats. Quality control.

**2. Chunking Strategy**

Choose chunk size carefully. 512-1024 tokens typical. Overlap for continuity. Consider semantic boundaries. Test different strategies.

**3. Embedding Quality**

Use appropriate embedding model. Match model to use case. Consider multilingual needs. Evaluate embedding quality. Update embeddings when needed.

**4. Vector Storage**

Choose appropriate vector database. Optimize for retrieval speed. Consider hybrid search. Index for performance. Monitor index health.

**5. Retrieval Strategy**

Use appropriate similarity metric. Combine with keyword search. Implement reranking. Consider user context. Optimize for recall/precision.

**6. Context Assembly**

Assemble retrieved context. Manage token budget. Prioritize relevant chunks. Add citations. Format for LLM.

**7. Generation with RAG**

Craft prompts with context. Instruct LLM to cite sources. Handle contradictions. Set appropriate temperature. Validate responses.

**8. Evaluation**

Measure retrieval quality. Evaluate generation quality. Use RAG metrics. A/B test strategies. Gather user feedback.

**9. Maintenance**

Update documents. Refresh embeddings. Monitor drift. Handle deletions. Maintain data quality.

**10. Scalability**

Design for document volume. Batch processing. Incremental updates. Distributed retrieval. Cost optimization.

### Checklist

- [ ] Document processing pipeline designed
- [ ] Chunking strategy selected
- [ ] Embedding model chosen
- [ ] Vector database configured
- [ ] Retrieval logic implemented
- [ ] Reranking strategy defined
- [ ] Prompt template designed
- [ ] Evaluation metrics set up
- [ ] Monitoring configured
- [ ] Update pipeline implemented

### Anti Pattern

**1. Poor Chunking** - Too large/small chunks, breaking semantic units, no overlap

**2. Single Retrieval** - No reranking, no hybrid search, no context weighting

**3. Ignoring Token Limits** - No context budget, exceeding LLM limits

**4. Stale Knowledge** - No update pipeline, outdated embeddings

**5. No Evaluation** - No retrieval/generation metrics

### Best Practice - Document Processing

```typescript
// services/document-processor.service.ts
import { RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter } from 'langchain/text_splitter';
import { PDFLoader } from 'langchain/document_loaders/fs/pdf';
import { DocxLoader } from 'langchain/document_loaders/fs/docx';

interface ProcessedDocument {
  id: string;
  chunks: DocumentChunk[];
  metadata: DocumentMetadata;
}

interface DocumentChunk {
  id: string;
  content: string;
  embedding?: number[];
  metadata: ChunkMetadata;
}

interface DocumentMetadata {
  source: string;
  title?: string;
  author?: string;
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
  type: 'pdf' | 'docx' | 'txt' | 'html';
}

interface ChunkMetadata {
  chunkIndex: number;
  totalChunks: number;
  charCount: number;
  tokenEstimate: number;
}

class DocumentProcessor {
  private textSplitter: RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter;
  private embeddingService: EmbeddingService;

  constructor(
    chunkSize: number = 1000,
    chunkOverlap: number = 200
  ) {
    this.textSplitter = new RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter({
      chunkSize,
      chunkOverlap,
      separators: ['\n\n', '\n', '. ', ' ', ''],
    });
    this.embeddingService = new EmbeddingService();
  }

  async processDocument(
    filePath: string,
    metadata: Partial<DocumentMetadata>
  ): Promise<ProcessedDocument> {
    const extension = filePath.split('.').pop()?.toLowerCase();
    let loader;

    switch (extension) {
      case 'pdf':
        loader = new PDFLoader(filePath);
        break;
      case 'docx':
        loader = new DocxLoader(filePath);
        break;
      default:
        loader = new TextLoader(filePath);
    }

    const docs = await loader.load();
    const fullText = docs.map(d => d.pageContent).join('\n\n');

    const chunks = await this.textSplitter.splitText(fullText);
    const embeddings = await this.embeddingService.createBatchEmbeddings(chunks);

    const processedChunks: DocumentChunk[] = chunks.map((content, index) => {
      const tokenEstimate = Math.ceil(content.length / 4);
      
      return {
        id: `${metadata.source}-chunk-${index}`,
        content,
        embedding: embeddings[index],
        metadata: {
          chunkIndex: index,
          totalChunks: chunks.length,
          charCount: content.length,
          tokenEstimate,
        },
      };
    });

    return {
      id: metadata.source || crypto.randomUUID(),
      chunks: processedChunks,
      metadata: {
        source: metadata.source || 'unknown',
        title: metadata.title,
        author: metadata.author,
        createdAt: metadata.createdAt || new Date(),
        updatedAt: new Date(),
        type: (extension || 'txt') as any,
      },
    };
  }

  async processText(
    text: string,
    source: string,
    additionalMetadata: Record<string, any> = {}
  ): Promise<ProcessedDocument> {
    const chunks = await this.textSplitter.splitText(text);
    const embeddings = await this.embeddingService.createBatchEmbeddings(chunks);

    const processedChunks: DocumentChunk[] = chunks.map((content, index) => ({
      id: `${source}-chunk-${index}`,
      content,
      embedding: embeddings[index],
      metadata: {
        chunkIndex: index,
        totalChunks: chunks.length,
        charCount: content.length,
        tokenEstimate: Math.ceil(content.length / 4),
      },
    }));

    return {
      id: source,
      chunks: processedChunks,
      metadata: {
        source,
        ...additionalMetadata,
        createdAt: new Date(),
        updatedAt: new Date(),
        type: 'txt' as const,
      },
    };
  }
}
```

### Best Practice - Vector Storage

```typescript
// services/vector-store.service.ts
import { Pinecone } from '@pinecone-database/pinecone';
import { supabase } from '@/lib/supabase';

interface VectorRecord {
  id: string;
  values: number[];
  metadata?: Record<string, any>;
}

interface RetrievalResult {
  id: string;
  score: number;
  content: string;
  metadata: Record<string, any>;
}

class VectorStore {
  private pinecone: Pinecone;
  private indexName: string;
  private useSupabase: boolean;

  constructor(useSupabase: boolean = false) {
    this.pinecone = new Pinecone({
      apiKey: process.env.PINECONE_API_KEY!,
    });
    this.useSupabase = useSupabase;
    this.indexName = process.env.PINECONE_INDEX || 'knowledge-base';
  }

  async upsertChunks(chunks: DocumentChunk[]): Promise<void> {
    if (this.useSupabase) {
      await this.upsertToSupabase(chunks);
    } else {
      await this.upsertToPinecone(chunks);
    }
  }

  private async upsertToPinecone(chunks: DocumentChunk[]): Promise<void> {
    const index = this.pinecone.Index(this.indexName);

    const vectors: VectorRecord[] = chunks.map(chunk => ({
      id: chunk.id,
      values: chunk.embedding || [],
      metadata: {
        content: chunk.content,
        ...chunk.metadata,
      },
    }));

    const batchSize = 100;
    for (let i = 0; i < vectors.length; i += batchSize) {
      const batch = vectors.slice(i, i + batchSize);
      await index.upsert(batch);
    }
  }

  private async upsertToSupabase(chunks: DocumentChunk[]): Promise<void> {
    const records = chunks.map(chunk => ({
      id: chunk.id,
      content: chunk.content,
      embedding: chunk.embedding,
      metadata: chunk.metadata,
    }));

    const { error } = await supabase
      .from('document_chunks')
      .upsert(records, { onConflict: 'id' });

    if (error) throw error;
  }

  async retrieve(
    queryEmbedding: number[],
    options: {
      topK?: number;
      filter?: Record<string, any>;
      namespace?: string;
    } = {}
  ): Promise<RetrievalResult[]> {
    if (this.useSupabase) {
      return this.retrieveFromSupabase(queryEmbedding, options);
    } else {
      return this.retrieveFromPinecone(queryEmbedding, options);
    }
  }

  private async retrieveFromPinecone(
    queryEmbedding: number[],
    options: { topK?: number; filter?: Record<string, any>; namespace?: string }
  ): Promise<RetrievalResult[]> {
    const index = this.pinecone.Index(this.indexName);
    
    const queryResponse = await index.query({
      vector: queryEmbedding,
      topK: options.topK || 10,
      filter: options.filter,
      namespace: options.namespace,
      includeMetadata: true,
    });

    return (queryResponse.matches || []).map(match => ({
      id: match.id,
      score: match.score || 0,
      content: match.metadata?.content || '',
      metadata: match.metadata || {},
    }));
  }

  private async retrieveFromSupabase(
    queryEmbedding: number[],
    options: { topK?: number; filter?: Record<string, any> }
  ): Promise<RetrievalResult[]> {
    const { data, error } = await supabase.rpc('match_documents', {
      query_embedding: queryEmbedding,
      match_threshold: 0.7,
      match_count: options.topK || 10,
    });

    if (error) throw error;

    return (data || []).map(row => ({
      id: row.id,
      score: row.similarity,
      content: row.content,
      metadata: row.metadata || {},
    }));
  }

  async deleteBySource(source: string): Promise<void> {
    if (this.useSupabase) {
      await supabase
        .from('document_chunks')
        .delete()
        .eq('metadata->>source', source);
    } else {
      const index = this.pinecone.Index(this.indexName);
      await index.deleteMany({ filter: { source } });
    }
  }
}
```

### Best Practice - RAG Generation

```typescript
// services/rag.service.ts
interface RAGOptions {
  query: string;
  maxContextTokens?: number;
  temperature?: number;
  model?: string;
  filters?: Record<string, any>;
}

interface RAGResponse {
  answer: string;
  sources: Array<{
    id: string;
    content: string;
    score: number;
    metadata: Record<string, any>;
  }>;
  tokensUsed: {
    prompt: number;
    completion: number;
  };
}

class RAGService {
  constructor(
    private retrievalService: RetrievalService,
    private llmService: ClaudeService | OpenAIService,
    private embeddingService: EmbeddingService,
    private maxContextTokens: number = 150000
  ) {}

  async query(options: RAGOptions): Promise<RAGResponse> {
    const {
      query,
      maxContextTokens = 120000,
      temperature = 0.3,
      model = 'claude-sonnet-4',
      filters
    } = options;

    const queryEmbedding = await this.embeddingService.createEmbedding(query);

    const retrieved = await this.retrievalService.retrieve({
      query,
      queryEmbedding,
      filters,
      maxResults: 20,
      rerank: true,
      rerankTopK: 10,
    });

    const context = this.assembleContext(retrieved, maxContextTokens - 2000);

    const systemPrompt = `You are a helpful AI assistant. Use the provided context to answer the user's question. Follow these rules:

1. Only use information from the provided context
2. If the context doesn't contain enough information, say so
3. Always cite your sources using [Source N] notation
4. Be concise but thorough
5. If you're uncertain, acknowledge it`;

    const userPrompt = `Context:
${context}

Question: ${query}

Answer the question based on the context above.`;

    const response = await this.llmService.createMessage(
      [
        { role: 'user', content: userPrompt }
      ],
      systemPrompt,
      { model, temperature, maxTokens: 2048 }
    );

    return {
      answer: response.content[0].text || response.choices?.[0]?.message?.content || '',
      sources: retrieved.slice(0, 5).map((r, i) => ({
        id: r.id,
        content: r.content.slice(0, 500) + (r.content.length > 500 ? '...' : ''),
        score: r.score,
        metadata: r.metadata,
      })),
      tokensUsed: {
        prompt: response.usage?.input_tokens || 0,
        completion: response.usage?.output_tokens || 0,
      },
    };
  }

  private assembleContext(
    results: RetrievalResult[],
    maxTokens: number
  ): string {
    const chunks: string[] = [];
    let totalTokens = 0;

    for (const result of results) {
      const tokenEstimate = Math.ceil(result.content.length / 4);
      
      if (totalTokens + tokenEstimate > maxTokens) {
        break;
      }

      chunks.push(`[Source ${chunks.length + 1}]: ${result.content}`);
      totalTokens += tokenEstimate;
    }

    return chunks.join('\n\n');
  }
}
```

